# What deploy/deploy-relay.sh reads from ../secrets/relay.env (never commit the real file).
RELAY_HOST=
# The relay runs on the server in Docker, reached only through its own Cloudflare Tunnel.
#
# Cloudflare → Networking → Tunnels → ferrocast-relay → token. The tunnel's public hostname
# ferrocast-relay.clearcraftlabs.com points to http://ferrocast-relay:8787, and so does
# tip.clearcraftlabs.com (tip pages: tip.clearcraftlabs.com/<name>, RELAY_TIP_URL), and
# remote.clearcraftlabs.com (Pro "Dashboard anywhere": phones open remote.clearcraftlabs.com/app/,
# RELAY_REMOTE_URL).
TUNNEL_TOKEN=
# kick.com → Settings → Developer → your app. Set its redirect URL to
#   https://ferrocast-relay.clearcraftlabs.com/v1/kick/callback
# and its webhook URL to
#   https://ferrocast-relay.clearcraftlabs.com/v1/kick/webhook
KICK_CLIENT_ID=
KICK_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Ferrocast Pro (Razorpay Subscriptions). These are NOT read from ../secrets/relay.env:
# deploy/razorpay-keys.sh writes them on the server (/opt/ferrocast-relay/relay.env) and
# deploy-relay.sh keeps them. Listed here so you know what the relay reads:
#   RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=rzp_live_…        the account's one key pair (shared with TransformX
#   RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=…             and Hookline: never regenerate it for Ferrocast)
#   RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=…         made by the script; pasted into Razorpay → Webhooks
#   RAZORPAY_PLAN_MONTHLY=plan_…      ₹199 a month, made by the script
#   RAZORPAY_PLAN_YEARLY=plan_…       ₹1,999 a year, made by the script
#   PRO_EMAIL_KEY=…                   keys the stored email hashes; made once, never changed
#   PRO_SALES_OPEN=false              true only once Pro's features exist
#   RELAY_VAULT_KEY=…                 32 bytes, base64: encrypts the secrets Pro keeps.
#                                     Made once on the server by deploy/vault-key.sh,
#                                     never changed, never printed
#   GOOGLE_TTS_KEY=AIza…              Ferrocast voices (Pro): a Google Cloud API key restricted
#                                     to the Text-to-Speech API. Unset: the voices are off.
#                                     Added by hand on the server (deploy/README.md), never logged
#   TTS_GLOBAL_MONTHLY_CHARS=800000   the voices' monthly cap for everyone together, checked
#                                     before Google is called. Keeps the bill at zero: Google's
#                                     free tier is 1,000,000 Neural2 characters a month, and the
#                                     relay never allows more than that whatever this says
#   CLOUDFLARE_AI_ACCOUNT_ID=…        Pro smart features on Cloudflare Workers AI's free tier
#   CLOUDFLARE_AI_TOKEN=…             (pro-keys.sh --ai; an account on the Workers Free plan, a
#                                     token with Workers AI Read). Unset: smart features are off
#   GEMINI_API_KEY=AIza…              Gemini's free tier, a key from a Google project WITHOUT
#                                     billing (one with billing is charged): the backup once
#                                     Cloudflare's free day is used up or it's down; alone, the provider
#   SMART_DAILY_CALLS=140             model calls a UTC day for everyone together (at most 1,000)
#   SMART_BACKUP_DAILY_CALLS=500      the backup's own calls a UTC day (at most 1,000)
#   RELAY_ADMIN_TOKEN=…               the Control Center's read-only stats (GET /admin/v1/stats),
#                                     32+ characters. Made on the server by control-center-key.sh,
#                                     which puts the same value in TransformX's .env.prod as
#                                     FERROCAST_ADMIN_TOKEN; never printed. Unset: the stats are off
# Optional, also on the server only:
#   RELAY_BLOB_DIR=/data/blobs        where Pro keeps files (default: next to the database)
#   RELAY_REMOTE_PEPPER=…             keys the stored hashes of phone tokens and pairing codes
#                                     (any long random text). Unset: derived from
#                                     RELAY_VAULT_KEY. Changing it signs every phone out
#
# Written by deploy-relay.sh itself (not secrets):
#   RELAY_REMOTE_URL=https://remote.clearcraftlabs.com   Pro "Dashboard anywhere": the phone's
#                                     page and its API (/app/, /r/…). Unset: the feature is off
#   RELAY_WEB_URL=https://ferrocast.clearcraftlabs.com   The website serving the dashboard (/app)
#                                     and the sign-in pages; it calls RELAY_REMOTE_URL across sites
#                                     (CORS for this origin only). After the move RELAY_REMOTE_URL
#                                     is https://api.clearcraftlabs.com
#   RELAY_REMOTE_ALIASES=https://remote.clearcraftlabs.com   Older web hosts still answered while
#                                     people move over (comma-separated origins), then removed
#   RELAY_DASHBOARD_DIR=/dashboard/current
#                                     the dashboard build phones get, copied by deploy-relay.sh
#   RELAY_OVERLAYS_DIR=/overlays/current
#                                     cloud mode's overlay pages, copied by deploy-relay.sh
#                                     from ../ferrocast-web/dist/dashboard to
#                                     /opt/ferrocast-relay/dashboard/releases/<date> with the
#                                     `current` link switched to it (mounted read-only)
#
# Accounts (docs/ACCOUNTS.md): email sign-in uses BREVO_API_KEY; Google sign-in needs both of
# these (pro-keys.sh --google, kept by deploy-relay.sh). Unset: Google answers 503 google_off.
#   RELAY_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=…apps.googleusercontent.com   OAuth client "Ferrocast accounts (web)",
#                                     redirect https://remote.clearcraftlabs.com/login/google/callback
#   RELAY_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=GOCSPX-…
#   RELAY_REMOTE_LOGIN=required       the web dashboard needs a signed-in account (default);
#                                     `optional` lets phones paired without one keep working
#
# The Ferrocast bot for Discord (Pro), also added on the server by hand and kept by
# deploy-relay.sh. discord.com/developers → Applications → Ferrocast (1561463863197835294).
# All four, or the bot is off (features.discord false); never logged:
#   DISCORD_APP_ID=1561463863197835294   General Information → Application ID
#   DISCORD_PUBLIC_KEY=…                 General Information → Public Key (64 hex characters)
#   DISCORD_CLIENT_SECRET=…              OAuth2 → Client Secret (bot install + viewer linking)
#   DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN=…                  Bot → Reset Token
# In the portal also set: OAuth2 → Redirects → https://ferrocast-relay.clearcraftlabs.com/discord/callback
# and General Information → Interactions Endpoint URL →
#   https://ferrocast-relay.clearcraftlabs.com/discord/interactions
#
# The weekly email (Pro), added on the server with pro-keys.sh --mail and kept by
# deploy-relay.sh; never logged. Unset: the weekly email is off (features.weekly_email false):
#   BREVO_API_KEY=xkeysib-…           Brevo → SMTP & API → API keys (not the SMTP key)
#   MAIL_FROM=Ferrocast <reports@mail.clearcraftlabs.com>   optional, the default shown
#   MAIL_TOKEN_KEY=…                  optional: signs confirm/unsubscribe links (any long
#                                     random text). Unset: derived from RELAY_VAULT_KEY
#   MAIL_DAILY_BUDGET=270             optional: emails a UTC day, relay-wide (confirms and
#                                     reports); keep it under the Brevo plan's daily limit
#
# The 24/7 cloud bot on Twitch (Pro), added on the server with pro-keys.sh --twitch and kept
# by deploy-relay.sh; never logged. A second, confidential Twitch app "Ferrocast Cloud" at
# dev.twitch.tv/console (OAuth Redirect URL https://ferrocast-relay.clearcraftlabs.com/v1/bot/twitch/callback,
# Category Chat Bot, Client Type Confidential). All three, or the Twitch cloud bot is off; it
# also needs RELAY_VAULT_KEY (the sign-ins are sealed). Kick's cloud bot uses KICK_CLIENT_ID /
# KICK_CLIENT_SECRET above (no extra setting):
#   TWITCH_CLOUD_CLIENT_ID=…          the Ferrocast Cloud app's Client ID
#   TWITCH_CLOUD_CLIENT_SECRET=…      same page → New Secret
#   TWITCH_CLOUD_EVENTSUB_SECRET=…    `openssl rand -hex 32`: signs EventSub's webhooks to
#                                     https://ferrocast-relay.clearcraftlabs.com/v1/bot/twitch/eventsub
#   TWITCH_CLOUD_DESKTOP_CLIENT_ID=…  optional: the desktop app's public Twitch client id (the
#                                     one releases are built with). A PC proves its channel
#                                     with a token of that app; defaults to the id this relay
#                                     was built with (FERROCAST_TWITCH_CLIENT_ID), else the
#                                     official app's
#
# The cloud bot on YouTube (Pro, a beta), added on the server with pro-keys.sh --youtube and
# kept by deploy-relay.sh; never logged. A Google OAuth client "Ferrocast Cloud" of type Web
# application (redirect https://ferrocast-relay.clearcraftlabs.com/v1/bot/youtube/callback,
# consent screen scope youtube.force-ssl; see deploy/README.md, incl. Google's verification).
# Both, plus RELAY_VAULT_KEY, or YouTube's cloud bot is off:
#   YOUTUBE_CLOUD_CLIENT_ID=…         …apps.googleusercontent.com
#   YOUTUBE_CLOUD_CLIENT_SECRET=…     GOCSPX-…
#   YOUTUBE_CLOUD_DAILY_UNITS_PER_SUB=9000  optional: YouTube quota units a subscription may
#                                     use a Pacific day (replies 50, live checks 1, reading 5)
#   YOUTUBE_CLOUD_DAILY_UNITS=9000    optional: units the whole relay may use a day (Google
#                                     gives a project 10,000 unless raised by its quota audit)
#   YOUTUBE_CLOUD_DESKTOP_CLIENT_ID=… optional: the desktop app's public Google client id
#                                     (defaults to the official one)
#   YOUTUBE_CLOUD_TIMER_GAP_MIN=15    optional: at most one cloud timer post on YouTube this
#                                     often, in minutes (each is 50 units; 0 = off, max 1440)
#
# Custom tip addresses (Pro): a streamer's own subdomain (tips.mychannel.com) shows their tip
# page through Cloudflare for SaaS on clearcraftlabs.com. Added on the server with
# pro-keys.sh --domains and kept by deploy-relay.sh; never logged. Both, plus RELAY_VAULT_KEY
# (it keys the streamer's TXT proof), or the feature is off (features.tip_domain false). The
# relay reads that TXT record over https://cloudflare-dns.com (outbound HTTPS). Setup
# (fallback origin, token, tunnel, the TXT proof) in deploy/README.md:
#   CF_SAAS_TOKEN=…                   an API token: Zone → SSL and Certificates → Edit (and
#                                     Custom Hostnames → Edit if listed), clearcraftlabs.com only
#   CF_ZONE_ID=…                      clearcraftlabs.com → Overview → API → Zone ID
